    <node id="n10">
        <data key="n_label">_Rational</data>
        <data key="n_package">core</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">value</data>
        <data key="n_url">developer.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">+ num: BigInt   (carries the sign)
+ den: BigInt   (always &gt; 0, may be unreduced)
+ add/subtract/multiply/divide/pow  (each takes a GcdPolicy)
+ approximate(maxDen): _Rational
+ approximateToDigits(digits): _Rational
+ maxBitLength: Int
__ companion __
+ of(n, d, policy): Option[_Rational]
+ fromDouble(d): Option[_Rational]  (exact dyadic)
DefaultPolicy = Threshold(256)      chosen by the 4.M benchmark
+ thresholdFor(digits) = max(256, 8 * digits)
sibling _Value of _Number (issue 4.L)
transcendentals via spire Real (core/Irrational)
_Number.unapply WIDENS to match this too:
case _Number(x) means: reads as real x
equality by cross-multiplication: 2/6 == 1/3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n11">
        <data key="n_label">GcdPolicy</data>
        <data key="n_package">core</data>
        <data key="n_kind">enum</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">data</data>
        <data key="n_url">developer.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">Eager             reduce on every construction
Lazy              never reduce (rejected by 4.M)
Threshold(maxBits) reduce past a bound (CHOSEN)</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n12">
        <data key="n_label">_Based</data>
        <data key="n_package">core</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">value</data>
        <data key="n_url">developer.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">+ value: Long
+ base: Int    (2..36)
+ balanced: Boolean
__ companion __
+ of(value, base, balanced): _Value
base 10 / non-int / radix outside 2..36 -&gt; _Number
fourth sibling of _Number (3.5); the base
lives on the VALUE so 0xFF still prints FF.
tag is SHALLOW: 0xFF + 1 -&gt; 256 (decimal)
toString: 0x.. / 0b.. / 0o.. / 0t.. / tobase(n,b)</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n13">
        <data key="n_label">_Interval</data>
        <data key="n_package">core</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">value</data>
        <data key="n_url">expressions.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">__ F_0008: rigorous bounds, outward rounding __
+ lo, hi: _Value  (both _Rational, or both _Number)
+ of(lo, hi): _Value  (lo == hi -&gt; the number)
fifth sibling of _Number, the first NOT widened:
every case _Number(x) misses it -&gt; symbolic
Double: TwoSum / TwoProduct, 1 ulp only if inexact
transcendental: 2 ulps; exact: spire at workingPrecision
add / multiply / divide / power / function / logBase
below / equal -&gt; Bool or unknown</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n14">
        <data key="n_label">LogicSemantics</data>
        <data key="n_package">core</data>
        <data key="n_kind">enum</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">data</data>
        <data key="n_url">logic.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">MinMax        min / max            (default)
Product       a*b / a+b-a*b
Lukasiewicz   max(0,a+b-1) / min(1,a+b)
the fuzzy t-norm/t-conorm family (issue 4.H)</data>
