    <node id="n113">
        <data key="n_label">_Cholesky</data>
        <data key="n_package">matrix</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">case</data>
        <data key="n_url">matrix.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">m : _Expression
__ chol(A) → L, A = L·Lᵀ (F_0054) __
dense: _MatrixValue.cholesky
exact: exactCholesky over the rationals
not square / symmetric / pos. definite → symbolic</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n114">
        <data key="n_label">Svd</data>
        <data key="n_package">matrix</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">utility</data>
        <data key="n_url">matrix.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">__ F_0061: svd(A[, full]) → [[U, S, V]], pinv, rank, cond __
kernel: _MatrixValue.svd, one-sided Jacobi, certified
_Svd (economy | full) · _PInv (a _MatrixOperation)
_Rank, _Cond: scalar results
__ F_0087: nullspace(A[, tol]) / orth(A[, tol]) __
_NullSpace(Subspace): bases at rank's rank; false if trivial
zero: σ ≤ 0.5·10^-p·σ_max (rank, pinv, nullspace, orth); cond: max(m,n)·ε
MaxSvdWork = max(m,n)·min(m,n)² ≤ 1e7 (Node-measured)</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n115">
        <data key="n_label">VectorProducts</data>
        <data key="n_package">matrix</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">utility</data>
        <data key="n_url">matrix.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">__ F_0160-F_0162: dot(u, v), cross(u, v), trace(A) __
__ F_0173: size(A), size(A, k) __
_Dot, _Trace, _SizeAlong: scalar results; _Cross, _Size: _MatrixOperations
size: shape read off the evaluated operand, in its tier; a number is 1x1
dot: no conjugate, a complex vector stays unevaluated
cross: right-handed, in u's shape
accumulated: a sum built term by term, refused
past MaxExpressionDepth when symbolic</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n116">
        <data key="n_label">Norm</data>
        <data key="n_package">matrix</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">utility</data>
        <data key="n_url">matrix.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">__ F_0039: norm(x[, 1 | 2 | inf | fro | p]) __
_Norm(x, NormOrder): a scalar result
the shape decides: row/column = vector
vector 2- and p-norms scaled by the largest modulus
matrix 2-norm = largest singular value, never eigen(A'A)</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n117">
