        <data key="n_members">Zoh    -- what sampled-data hardware does
Tustin -- bilinear, exactly invertible
Foh, ImpulseInvariant, MatchedPoleZero,
ForwardEuler, BackwardEuler (F_0009)
ALWAYS an explicit argument: two methods give
DIFFERENT discrete poles</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n188">
        <data key="n_label">Discretisation</data>
        <data key="n_package">control</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">object</data>
        <data key="n_url">control.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">c2d: Tustin = substitution;
Zoh = step response -&gt; sample -&gt; ztrans
-&gt; (1 - z^-1) factor   [needs 6.33]
ZOH time / index vars come from
freshVar, never literal names: a
literal would capture a plant
parameter of the same name (2.12)
Foh / impulse: ramp / impulse response, same route
matched: roots by e^(sTs), gain at low frequency
Euler: substitutions; c2dPrewarped: Tustin at w
d2c: Tustin and Euler; the rest would need a
logarithm -&gt; declined</data>
    </node>
