        <data key="n_members">__ F_0065: DARE, LQR, Lyapunov, Kalman __
dare / dlqr (u = -K x) / dlyap / kalmanGain
kalmanStep: update, then predict (Joseph form)
structure-preserving doubling, certified by
its residual; the STABILISING solution only
declines: not stabilisable / detectable, Q or R
not definite, shapes, n &gt; 200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n198">
        <data key="n_label">Elimination</data>
        <data key="n_package">optimize</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">utility</data>
        <data key="n_url">optimization.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">eliminate(eqs, unknowns): EVERY real solution
or None -- never a partial list
1. linear, constant coefficient: substitute (exact)
2. one unknown left: every real root
(square-free parts, the 2.5 rule)
3. linear, coefficient c in other unknowns:
divide AND branch on c = 0 -- dividing
alone silently drops those solutions
4. steps declined or none applies: a lex
Groebner basis, then the steps (F_0068)
an inexact root: withoutRounding first
every candidate verified against the originals
MaxEliminationSteps = 4000 (measured)</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n199">
        <data key="n_label">Groebner</data>
        <data key="n_package">optimize</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">utility</data>
        <data key="n_url">optimization.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">__ F_0068 __
groebnerBasis(eqs, unknowns, env): reduced, lex
Buchberger, EXACT rationals always (spire)
caps: basis 40, degree 24, 4096 bits, 2000 work
withoutRounding: drop rounding-level coefficients</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n200">
        <data key="n_label">Stationary</data>
        <data key="n_package">optimize</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">utility</data>
        <data key="n_url">optimization.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">stationaryPoints: solve grad f = 0
classifyStationary: Hessian eigenvalue signs
(relative zero test; Degenerate = unknown)
lagrangePoints: multipliers from freshVar</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n201">
        <data key="n_label">Convexity</data>
        <data key="n_package">optimize</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">utility</data>
        <data key="n_url">optimization.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">true: EVERY PRINCIPAL minor provably &gt;= 0
(leading minors prove definiteness only)
and f defined everywhere
false: a WITNESS -- a minor provably &lt; 0, or a
grid point where f is real and curvature &lt; 0
else symbolic</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n202">
        <data key="n_label">KKT</data>
        <data key="n_package">optimize</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">utility</data>
        <data key="n_url">optimization.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">kktConditions: STATED as and/=/&lt;=/&gt;=
(min f, g &lt;= 0, h = 0; mu, lambda via freshVar)
kktPoints: 2^m active sets over Elimination
MaxKKTInequalities = 10 (measured)</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n203">
        <data key="n_label">Minimize</data>
        <data key="n_package">optimize</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">utility</data>
        <data key="n_url">optimization.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">gd | newton | bfgs | pbfgs -- ALWAYS named
pbfgs = PROJECTED BFGS, not L-BFGS-B (R_0069)
answer only if stationarity = sum|g_i||x_i - x0_i| / (f(x0) - f(x))
passes 0.5*10^-precision (scale-free, F_0095); else Left(MinimizeFailure)
MaxMinimizeIterations = 2000 (measured)</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n204">
        <data key="n_label">QP</data>
        <data key="n_package">optimize</data>
        <data key="n_kind">class</data>
        <data key="n_stereotype">utility</data>
        <data key="n_url">optimization.html</data>
        <data key="n_members">qpSolve(H, f, ineq, eq, lb, ub, warm, env)
min 1/2 z'Hz + f'z, A z &lt;= b, Aeq z = beq, bounds
Goldfarb-Idnani dual active set when H positive DEFINITE;
semidefinite H: primal active set from an lpSolve vertex (F_0074)
KKT-certified at 0.5*10^-precision, relative
Left(QpFailure) / Right(QpResult incl. active set)
QpResult.multipliers: QpMultipliers (F_0066)
MaxQpIterations 2000, MaxQpVariables 500 (measured)</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n205">
        <data key="n_label">Nlp</data>
